{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the determinant of the reflection matrix \\(\\mathbf{R}\\) over the vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Normalize the vector**: The vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix}\\) can be normalized to \\(\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\end{pmatrix}\\).\n\n2. **Find the reflection matrix**: The reflection matrix \\(\\mathbf{R}\\) over a vector \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} u_1 \\\\ u_2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{R} = \\mathbf{I} - 2 \\mathbf{u} \\mathbf{u}^T\n   \\]\n   where \\(\\mathbf{I}\\) is the identity matrix and \\(\\mathbf{u} \\mathbf{u}^T\\) is the outer product of \\(\\mathbf{u}\\) with itself. For \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\end{pmatrix}\\), we have:\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{u} \\mathbf{u}^T = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}} & \\frac{5}{\\sqrt{26}} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{26} & \\frac{5}{26} \\\\ \\frac{5}{26} & \\frac{25}{26} \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n   Therefore,\n   \\[\n   \\mathbf{R} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} - 2 \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{1}{26} & \\frac{5}{26} \\\\ \\frac{5}{26} & \\frac{25}{26} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{2}{26} & \\frac{10}{26} \\\\ \\frac{10}{26} & \\frac{50}{26} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{24}{26} & -\\frac{10}{26} \\\\ -\\frac{10}{26} & -\\frac{24}{26} \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{12}{13} & -\\frac{5}{13} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{13} & -\\frac{12}{13} \\end{pmatrix}\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":1589,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,86960,315,279,21844,6172,1124,11520,1